 "result_text": "I fixed the bad fractional part in `SubstationFormat.ms_to_timestamp` in `pysubs2/substation.py`. I checked the function directly but did not run the test suite or the CLI on your example file.\n\nThe old code split the time into hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds first. It then rounded the milliseconds to centiseconds. A value like 39,996 ms rounded up to 100 centiseconds, so it printed as `39.100` instead of carrying into the seconds. The fix rounds to the nearest centisecond before splitting.\n\nQuick checks on the function:\n- 39,996 ms now gives `0:00:40.00`, which is the case from your report.\n- 39,994 ms still gives `0:00:39.99`.",
